{"id":"44e2654677eb387be9dc09b3cb1d3112affefee9","axis":"silent","repo":"vercel/turbo","sha":"44e2654677eb387be9dc09b3cb1d3112affefee9","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"apps/docs/content/docs/reference/configuration.mdx","lines":["@@ -308,6 +308,24 @@ Enable experimental features that will become the default behavior in future ver","   cache](/docs/crafting-your-repository/caching)."," </Callout>"," ","+#### `hashFilePermissions`","+","+Default: `false`","+","+Include executable permissions in file hashes for task inputs and global dependencies. With this flag enabled, changing an input file from non-executable to executable, or back, changes the task hash even when its contents stay the same.","+","+On Unix, a regular file is executable if any owner, group, or other executable bit is set. On Windows, regular files are treated as non-executable. Symlink permissions and read or write permission bits do not affect hashes.","+","+Enabling this flag changes all task hashes. Existing cache entries are not reused. With the flag disabled, Turborepo preserves content-only file hashing.","+","+```jsonc title=\"./turbo.json\"","+{","+  \"futureFlags\": {","+    \"hashFilePermissions\": true,","+  },","+}","+```","+"," #### `errorsOnlyShowHash`"," "," Default: `false`"],"additions":18,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/turborepo-filewatch/src/hash_watcher.rs","lines":["@@ -1649,7 +1649,12 @@ mod tests {","         let (query_tx, query_rx) = tokio::sync::mpsc::channel(1);","         let (exit_tx, exit_rx) = tokio::sync::oneshot::channel();","         let (file_event_tx, file_events) = WatchSource::channel();","-        let subscriber = Subscriber::new(repo_root, package_discovery_rx, SCM::Manual, query_rx);","+        let subscriber = Subscriber::new(","+            repo_root,","+            package_discovery_rx,","+            SCM::Manual(turborepo_scm::FileHashMode::ContentOnly),","+            query_rx,","+        );","         let handle = tokio::spawn(subscriber.w